 "template": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new quotation (New button on the Orders/Quotations list). Set the Customer field to '{{v1}}' by typing the name and choosing the matching option from the autocomplete dropdown (it must be actually selected from the dropdown, not just typed). Then add exactly ONE order line: in the Order Lines table, pick any product from the product catalogue by typing in the product field and choosing an option from the autocomplete dropdown, and set its Quantity to 3. Let Odoo auto-fill the unit price. Do NOT confirm the quotation yet — leave it as a draft quotation. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price Odoo filled in for that line, (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes, and (d) the quotation's reference name (e.g. S00042) if shown.",
